# Coding Guidelines

## Developer Profile

Experienced developer - assume strong understanding of concepts

## Code Style

- Concise over verbose
- Self-documenting code > comments
- YAGNI principle
- Show, don't explain
- Namespaces: Maximum depth of two levels (one dot separator)

## Documentation

- READMEs: Only essentials (usage, 1-2 examples max, extension points)
- Location: Feature-specific docs should be README.md files in the same folder as the code
- Comments: Only for complex logic or non-obvious decisions
- Avoid: Extensive examples, obvious explanations, step-by-step tutorials, feature lists, benefits sections
